{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:06:48.196Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"web_search_end","call_id":"exec-92864035-1113-4de3-be64-1c0761d18329","query":"PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT 6.3.10 general purpose bit 11 filename UTF-8 official ...","action":{"type":"search","queries":["PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT 6.3.10 general purpose bit 11 filename UTF-8 official","site:pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT language encoding flag bit 11"]},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"support.pkware.com","ref_id":"turn28search0","snippet":"ZIP file format by third party development organizations, PKWARE® remains committed to the periodic publication of the APPNOTE specification. ... The current general released version","title":"Publication Policy","url":"https://support.pkware.com/pkzip/publication-policy"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"support.pkware.com","ref_id":"turn28search1","snippet":"www.pkware.com/documents/APPNOTE/APPNOTE_6.2.0.txt ... APPNOTE-6.3.10. ... APPNOTE-6.3.8.","title":"Application Note Archives","url":"https://support.pkware.com/pkzip/application-note-archives"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"gist.github.com","ref_id":"turn28search2","snippet":"# ross-spencer/PKZIP APPNOTE 6.3.4. ... Unmodified copy of PKZIP Speciffication, source date: 1 November 2015: https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT ... | filename and comment mu","title":"Unmodified copy of PKZIP Speciffication, source date: 1 November 2015: https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/ross-spencer/386965c55359d86e7c59"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"gist.github.com","ref_id":"turn28search3","snippet":"| -Added option for Unicode filename ... | 6.3.1 -Corrected standard hash values for 04/11/2007 ... | values for UTF-8 file name and ... |","title":"Unmodified copy of PKZIP Speciffication, source date: 1 November 2015: https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/danicat/207ce39725fc0513bba8ba553e868bb8"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.conbu.jp","ref_id":"turn28search4","snippet":"出典はPKWARE APPNOTE.TXT Version 6.3.10(Revised Nov 01, 2022)の§4.4.4 general purpose bit flagとAPPENDIX Dです。 ... ビット11ありは「UTF-8でMUST(必須)エンコード」、ビット11なしは「従来のZIP文字エンコーディング(IBM Code Page 437)にSHOULD(努力目標であり必須","title":"ZIPで日本語ファイル名が文字化けする理由|ファイル名・パス制限の横断早見表","url":"https://www.conbu.jp/tool/filename-limits/article-zip-mojibake.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"support.pkware.com","ref_id":"turn28search5","snippet":"This new format combined data compression, file management, and data encryption within a portable archive format. ... The APPNOTE provides developers a general description and","title":"APPNOTE","url":"https://support.pkware.com/pkzip/appnote"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.loc.gov","ref_id":"turn28search6","snippet":"Changes between version 6.3.2 (2007) and version 6.3.3 (2012) of APPNOTE.TXT do not reflect changes in the format, but rather editorial and layout changes based","title":"ZIP File Format (PKWARE)","url":"https://www.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000354.shtml"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"support.pkware.com","ref_id":"turn28search12","snippet":"PKWARE in a file called APPNOTE.TXT.","title":"Technical Note – ZIP File Capacities","url":"https://support.pkware.com/__attachments/8127162/Technical%20Note%20-%20ZIP%20File%20Capacities-r2.pdf?inst-v=0a14903e-c3b8-4170-8b9c-966c4ecbcf9d"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"gist.github.com","ref_id":"turn28search7","snippet":"Backup of the APPNOTE.TXT file via https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT cited in Python's zipfile module ... | -Added option for Unicode filename ... | 6.3.5 -Documented compres","title":"Backup of the APPNOTE.TXT file via https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT cited in Python's zipfile module · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/lmmx/114deec9787ffb4e2ad35f55f63d48a1"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"gist.github.com","ref_id":"turn28search8","snippet":"Version: 6.3.10 https://support.pkware.com/display/PKZIP/APPNOTE ... general purpose bit flag | 6 | 2 bytes | link","title":"ZIPの仕様を日本語でまとめる (ysakasin/zip.md より ZIP64およびマルチボリューム関連を中心に加筆。ysakasinさんに感謝) · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/rougemeilland/92c2e6ecdfcc61ed5665f0a75c866a95"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"wwws.loc.gov","ref_id":"turn28search9","snippet":"Over the years the format has been extended by PKWARE to adapt to new expectations of users and to changing technology, for example, to allow","title":"ZIP File Format (PKWARE)","url":"https://wwws.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000354.shtml"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.conbu.jp","ref_id":"turn28search10","snippet":"汎用フラグ ビット11(Language encoding flag/EFS)を立てると、ファイル名とコメントはUTF-8でMUST(必須)エンコード ... 出典: PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT §4.4.4 general purpose bit flag ... 出典: PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT(規定)+ この環境での python 実機再現","title":"ZIPの文字コードと文字化けの条件|ファイル名・パス制限の横断早見表","url":"https://www.conbu.jp/tool/filename-limits/zip.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"support.pkware.com","ref_id":"turn28search11","snippet":"* PKWARE Support ... High-performance encryption and compression software ... * ### PK Transparent Server Agent - Public","title":"PKWARE Support","url":"https://support.pkware.com/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"ptacts.uspto.gov","ref_id":"turn28search13","snippet":"The Java platform does not support encryption. ... Details on the use of ZIP in OPC are in section 10 and Annex C of ISO/IEC","title":"ZIP File Format (PKWARE)","url":"https://ptacts.uspto.gov/ptacts/public-informations/petitions/1520098/download-documents?REDACTED"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"citeseerx.ist.psu.edu","ref_id":"turn28search14","snippet":"ZIP Appnote.txt ClarificationsBit ... section describing the Strong Encryption ... Table C–6, “Support for Extra field (variable size), PKWARE-reserved”, specifies the detailed production, ... 3Appnot","title":"Office Open","url":"https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=664fbfd9ec9de0ee00b3fda8d90d9f347dd675b3&repid=rep1&type=pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"generationkpmg.pl","ref_id":"turn28search15","snippet":"- 2.0: (1993)[11] File entries can be compressed with DEFLATE and use traditional PKWARE encryption (ZipCrypto). ... - 4.5: (2001)[12] Documented 64-bit zip format. ...","title":"The .ZIP file format specification is formally named \"APPNOTE -.ZIP File Format Specification\" and it is published on the PKWARE.com website since the late 1990s.[11] Several versions of the specification were not published. Specifications of some features such as BZIP2 compression, strong encryption specification and others were published by PKWARE a few years after their creation. The URL of the online specification was changed several times on the PKWARE website. A summary of key advances in various versions of the PKWARE specification:","url":"https://generationkpmg.pl/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Wonders_of_ZIP_file_format.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn28search16","snippet":"Specifications of some features such as BZIP2 compression, strong encryption specification and others were published by PKWARE a few years after their creation. ... *","title":"ZIP (file format)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZIP_%28file_format%29"}]}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:06:48.210Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03185-3392-7c92-953c-c1477893331d","call_id":"call_P0fLfONWdug6KVWitWUmfWoO","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Publication Policy (https://support.pkware.com/pkzip/publication-policy)\nciteturn28search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; ZIP file format by third party development organizations, PKWARE® remains committed to the periodic publication of the APPNOTE specification. ... The current general released version of the APPNOTE will retain the file name APPNOTE.TXT.\n\n# Publication Policy\n\n## ZIP File Format Specification Publication Policy\n\nIn order to ensure the interoperability of the .ZIP file format by third party development organizations, PKWARE® remains committed to the periodic publication of the APPNOTE specification. The publication of changes and revisions to this specification will occur on the following schedule:\n\n \n\nNotification of Change\n\nWhen feature changes affecting the .ZIP file format are identified, a preliminary release of this information will be made within 120 days following the general release of the first product in which these changes are implemented. This preliminary information will identify areas of current or planned changes to allow third party developers to avoid any conflicts with their development activities.\n\nFinal Publication\n\nFinal publication of feature changes to the specification will occur within nine months of the general release of the last product in which these changes are implemented. The availability of the final release of the specification will be timed to ensure the changes work reliably and conflict-free across all supported operating environments.\n\nNaming Convention\n\nThe current general released version of the APPNOTE will retain the file name APPNOTE.TXT. Draft copies will be named a APPNOTE-x.y.z-DRAFT.txt. Archived copies will be named APPNOTE-x.y.z.TXT.\n\n1 x, y, and z represent the version major, minor and step version.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nApplication Note Archives (https://support.pkware.com/pkzip/application-note-archives)\nciteturn28search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 22.3 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; www.pkware.com/documents/APPNOTE/APPNOTE_6.2.0.txt ... APPNOTE-6.3.10. ... APPNOTE-6.3.8.\n\n# Application Note Archives\n\nThis page provides a fixed location for APPNOTE reference and change history.\n\nSpecific versions of the APPNOTE named within other published specifications are posted here for reference.\n\n6.2.0 – 04/26/2004\n\nThis version is provided in support of ECMA-376 and ISO/IEC 29500, the standards for Office Open XML File Formats. These document standards incorporate ZIP technology based on this specification.\nTo download APPNOTE version 6.2.0, Click Here or copy and paste the following URL into your browser window:\nwww.pkware.com/documents/APPNOTE/APPNOTE_6.2.0.txt\n\nOther Archived Versions: \n\nAPPNOTE-6.3.10.TXT\n\nAPPNOTE-6.3.9.TXT\n\nAPPNOTE-6.3.8.TXT\n\nAPPNOTE-6.3.7.TXT\n\nAPPNOTE-6.3.6.TXT\n\nAPPNOTE-6.3.5.TXT\nAPPNOTE-6.3.4.TXT\nAPPNOTE-6.3.3.TXT\nAPPNOTE-6.3.0.TXT\nAPPNOTE-6.2.0.TXT\nAPPNOTE-5.2.0.TXT\nAPPNOTE-4.5.0.TXT\nAPPNOTE-2.0.TXT\nAPPNOTE-1.0.TXT--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnmodified copy of PKZIP Speciffication, source date: 1 November 2015: https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT · GitHub (https://gist.github.com/ross-spencer/386965c55359d86e7c59)\nciteturn28search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.8 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; # ross-spencer/PKZIP APPNOTE 6.3.4. ... Unmodified copy of PKZIP Speciffication, source date: 1 November 2015: https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT ...  | filename and comment must support The Unicode Standard, Version 4.1.0 or ...  | whether \"modified-UTF-8\" (JAVA) is used, or UTF-8-MAC. ...  | D.5 General purpose bit 11 will not imply any encoding of file content or\n | \n | APPENDIX D - Language Encoding (EFS)\n | ------------------------------------\n | \n | D.1 The ZIP format has historically supported only the original IBM PC character\n | encoding set, commonly referred to as IBM Code Page 437. This limits storing\n | file name characters to only those within the original MS-DOS range of values\n | and does not properly support file names in other character encodings, or\n | languages. To address this limitation, this specification will support the\n | following change.\n | \n | D.2 If general purpose bit 11 is unset, the file name and comment should conform\n | to the original ZIP character encoding. If general purpose bit 11 is set, the\n | filename and comment must support The Unicode Standard, Version 4.1.0 or\n | greater using the character encoding form defined by the UTF-8 storage\n | specification. The Unicode Standard is published by the The Unicode\n | Consortium (www.unicode.org). UTF-8 encoded data stored within ZIP files\n | is expected to not include a byte order mark (BOM).\n | \n | D.3 Applications may choose to supplement this file name storage through the use\n | of the 0x0008 Extra Field. Storage for this optional field is currently\n | undefined, however it will be used to allow storing extended information\n | on source or target encoding that may further assist applications with file\n | name, or file content encoding tasks. Please contact PKWARE with any\n | requirements on how this field should be used.\n | \n | D.4 The 0x0008 Extra Field storage may be used with either setting for general\n | purpose bit 11. Examples of the intended usage for this field is to store\n | whether \"modified-UTF-8\" (JAVA) is used, or UTF-8-MAC. Similarly, other\n | commonly used character encoding (code page) designations can be indicated\n | through this field. Formalized values for use of the 0x0008 record remain\n | undefined at this time. The definition for the layout of the 0x0008 field\n | will be published when available. Use of the 0x0008 Extra Field provides\n | for storing data within a ZIP file in an encoding other than IBM Code\n | Page 437 or UTF-8.\n | \n | D.5 General purpose bit 11 will not imply any encoding of file content or\n | password. Values defining character encoding for file content or\n | password must be stored within the 0x0008 Extended Language Encoding\n | Extra Field.\n | \n | D.6 Ed Gordon of the Info-ZIP group has defined a pair of \"extra field\" records\n | that can be used to store UTF-8 file name and file comment fields. These\n | records can be used for cases when the general purpose bit 11 method\n | for storing UTF-8 data in the standard file name and comment fields is\n | not desirable. A common case for this alternate method is if backward\n | compatibility with older programs is required.\n | \n | D.7 Definitions for the record structure of these fields are included above\n | in the section on 3rd party mappings for \"extra field\" records. These\n | records are identified by Header ID's 0x6375 (Info-ZIP Unicode Comment\n | Extra Field) and 0x7075 (Info-ZIP Unicode Path Extra Field).\n | \n | D.8 The choice of which storage method to use when writing a ZIP file is left\n | to the implementation. Developers should expect that a ZIP file may\n | contain either method and should provide support for reading data in\n | either format. Use of general purpose bit 11 reduces storage requirements\n | for file name data by not requiring additional \"extra field\" data for\n | each file, but can result in older ZIP programs not being able to extract\n | files. Use of the 0x6375 and 0x7075 records will result in a ZIP file\n | that should always be readable by older ZIP programs, but requires more\n | storage per file to write file name and/or file comment fields.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnmodified copy of PKZIP Speciffication, source date: 1 November 2015: https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT · GitHub (https://gist.github.com/danicat/207ce39725fc0513bba8ba553e868bb8)\nciteturn28search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.3 years ago; Crawled: last month;  | -Added option for Unicode filename ...  | 6.3.1 -Corrected standard hash values for 04/11/2007 ...  | values for UTF-8 file name and ...  | easier referencing of this APPNOTE ...  | Bit 6: Strong encryption. ...  | Bit 11: Language encoding flag (EFS). ...  | 10 - PKWARE Data Compression Library Imploding (old IBM TERSE)\nRefer to the\n | section in this document entitled \"Incorporating PKWARE\n | Proprietary Technology into Your Product\" for more\n | information.\n | \n | Bit 7: Currently unused.\n | \n | Bit 8: Currently unused.\n | \n | Bit 9: Currently unused.\n | \n | Bit 10: Currently unused.\n | \n | Bit 11: Language encoding flag (EFS). If this bit is set,\n | the filename and comment fields for this file\n | MUST be encoded using UTF-8. (see APPENDIX D)\n | \n | Bit 12: Reserved by PKWARE for enhanced compression.\n | \n | Bit 13: Set when encrypting the Central Directory to indicate\n | selected data values in the Local Header are masked to\n | hide their actual values. See the section describing\n | the Strong Encryption Specification for details. Refer\n | to the section in this document entitled \"Incorporating\n | PKWARE Proprietary Technology into Your Product\" for\n | more information.\n | \n | Bit 14: Reserved by PKWARE.\n | \n | Bit 15: Reserved by PKWARE.\n | \n | 4.4.5 compression method: (2 bytes)\n | \n | 0 - The file is stored (no compression)\n | 1 - The file is Shrunk\n | 2 - The file is Reduced with compression factor 1\n | 3 - The file is Reduced with compression factor 2\n | 4 - The file is Reduced with compression factor 3\n | 5 - The file is Reduced with compression factor 4\n | 6 - The file is Imploded\n | 7 - Reserved for Tokenizing compression algorithm\n | 8 - The file is Deflated\n | 9 - Enhanced Deflating using Deflate64(tm)\n | 10 - PKWARE Data Compression Library Imploding (old IBM TERSE)\n | 11 - Reserved by PKWARE\n | 12 - File is compressed using BZIP2 algorithm\n | 13 - Reserved by PKWARE\n | 14 - LZMA (EFS)\n | 15 - Reserved by PKWARE\n | 16 - Reserved by PKWARE\n | 17 - Reserved by PKWARE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIPで日本語ファイル名が文字化けする理由|ファイル名・パス制限の横断早見表 (https://www.conbu.jp/tool/filename-limits/article-zip-mojibake.html)\nciteturn28search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 weeks ago; Crawled: last week; 出典はPKWARE APPNOTE.TXT Version 6.3.10(Revised Nov 01, 2022)の§4.4.4 general purpose bit flagとAPPENDIX Dです。 ... ビット11ありは「UTF-8でMUST(必須)エンコード」、ビット11なしは「従来のZIP文字エンコーディング(IBM Code Page 437)にSHOULD(努力目標であり必須ではない)準拠」とされています。\n\n20バイト/28バイト「日本語ファイル名.txt」をCP932/UTF-8で符号化した際のバイト数(python実測)\n\nMUST/SHOULDビット11あり(UTF-8)となし(CP437)で異なる義務の強さ\n\n## ZIPのファイル名エンコーディングを決める1ビット\n\n出典はPKWARE APPNOTE.TXT Version 6.3.10(Revised Nov 01, 2022)の§4.4.4 general purpose bit flagとAPPENDIX Dです。汎用フラグのビット11(0x0800、Language encoding flag/EFSとも呼ばれます)が立っている場合、原文には次のようにあります。\n\n> MUST be encoded using UTF-8\n\n一方、このビットが立っていない場合、APPENDIX Dは次のように定めています。\n\n> SHOULD conform to the original ZIP\n\nここで見落とせないのは、両者の義務の強さが非対称であることです。ビット11ありは「UTF-8でMUST(必須)エンコード」、ビット11なしは「従来のZIP文字エンコーディング(IBM Code Page 437)にSHOULD(努力目標であり必須ではない)準拠」とされています。つまりビット11が立っていないZIPのファイル名は、規格上は前提としてCP437として解釈される、という約束事になっています。\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPPNOTE (https://support.pkware.com/pkzip/appnote)\nciteturn28search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago; This new format combined data compression, file management, and data encryption within a portable archive format. ... The APPNOTE provides developers a general description and technical details of the . ... ZIP standard, please join the PKWARE APPNOTE subscription service.\n\n# APPNOTE\n\nQuick Link: .ZIP Application Note\n\n## .ZIP Application Note\n\nPKWARE® introduced the ZIP format in 1989. This new format combined data compression, file management, and data encryption within a portable archive format. ZIP quickly became the accepted industry standard for cross-platform data exchange and efficient data storage. In order to ensure the continued interoperability of the .ZIP file format for all users, PKWARE publishes an Application Note on the .ZIP file format. The APPNOTE provides developers a general description and technical details of the .ZIP specification. This specification is maintained and periodically updated by PKWARE with support from interested industry experts and other users of this format. These changes are intended to include new capabilities in anticipation of the emerging needs of the ZIP community, while ensuring on-going interoperability for ZIP files.  If your developing applications using the .--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIP File Format (PKWARE) (https://www.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000354.shtml)\nciteturn28search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Changes between version 6.3.2 (2007) and version 6.3.3 (2012) of APPNOTE.TXT do not reflect changes in the format, but rather editorial and layout changes based on discussions with an ISO working group that studied the ZIP format. ... Features that do tend to get incorporated include: long filenames, encoding of filenames, etc. in UTF-8, and the ZIP64 mechanism introduced by PKWARE for handling large ZIP files. ... The compilers of this resource are not aware of any patent concerns with compression or encryption methods for which the ZIP_PK specification through version 6.3.3 of APPNOTE.TXT, has identifying codes. ...     * 10 best Android file explorer apps, file browsers, and file managers!\nZIP Application Note with a file name of APPNOTE.TXT.\n    Documentation  | In the past, PKWARE provided public access only to the most recent Application Note. In association with the standardization of Office Open XML (OOXML) as ISO 29500:2008, access was also provided to the version 6.2.0 explicitly incorporated into that format specification. PKWARE now provides access to an archive of selected versions of the .ZIP Application Note. See Notes below for a chronology of versions of APPNOTE.TXT introducing significant new features to the format. Changes between version 6.3.2 (2007) and version 6.3.3 (2012) of APPNOTE.TXT do not reflect changes in the format, but rather editorial and layout changes based on discussions with an ISO working group that studied the ZIP format. Changes, such as adding paragraph numbers, were made to making it easier for ISO standards to reference the ZIP specification in an unambiguous and reliable way.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTechnical Note – ZIP File Capacities (https://support.pkware.com/__attachments/8127162/Technical%20Note%20-%20ZIP%20File%20Capacities-r2.pdf?inst-v=0a14903e-c3b8-4170-8b9c-966c4ecbcf9d)\nciteturn28search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; PKWARE in a file called APPNOTE.TXT.\nTechnical Note – ZIP File Capacities \n \n \nDate issued:  | 08-01-2014  | Notice sent to:  | PKWARE Technical Support, Sales\nEngineers; Customer’s, Prospects\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nEffective date:  | Immediately  | Products affected:  |  PKZIP/SecureZIP All Platforms\nTechnical Support\nTicket ID:  | N/A  | Location of completed fix:  | N/A\nAuthor:  | JPeterson  |  | Author:  \nJPeterson \n \n \n \n \nShort description of issue:   This note documents a number of important ZIP file capacities \nsuch as how large a ZIP file can be, how many files it can contain, and other storage related \nlimits applicable to .ZIP files.  This information affects PKSFX capacities also.  These \ncapacities affect PKZIP and SecureZIP as well as all other ZIP compatible applications that conform \nto the published specification for .ZIP files.   \n \nThe specification for the .ZIP file format has been publicly available and distributed by \nPKWARE in a file called APPNOTE.TXT.  The APPNOTE documents the internal data \nstructures and layout that define a .--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBackup of the APPNOTE.TXT file via https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT cited in Python's zipfile module · GitHub (https://gist.github.com/lmmx/114deec9787ffb4e2ad35f55f63d48a1)\nciteturn28search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.2 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Backup of the APPNOTE.TXT file via https://pkware.cachefly.net/webdocs/casestudies/APPNOTE.TXT cited in Python's zipfile module ...  | -Added option for Unicode filename ...  | 6.3.5 -Documented compression methods 16 11/31/2018 ...  | Bit 6: Strong encryption. ...  | Bit 11: Language encoding flag (EFS). ...  | MUST be encoded using UTF-8. (see APPENDIX D) ...  | 10 - PKWARE Data Compression Library Imploding (old IBM TERSE) ...  | If bit 3 of the general purpose flag is set, this\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIPの仕様を日本語でまとめる (ysakasin/zip.md より ZIP64およびマルチボリューム関連を中心に加筆。ysakasinさんに感謝) · GitHub (https://gist.github.com/rougemeilland/92c2e6ecdfcc61ed5665f0a75c866a95)\nciteturn28search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Version: 6.3.10 https://support.pkware.com/display/PKZIP/APPNOTE ... general purpose bit flag  | 6  | 2 bytes  | link\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIP File Format (PKWARE) (https://wwws.loc.gov/preservation/digital/formats/fdd/fdd000354.shtml)\nciteturn28search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; Over the years the format has been extended by PKWARE to adapt to new expectations of users and to changing technology, for example, to allow improved methods for compression and encryption, to support larger file sizes, and to support UNICODE UTF-8 for filenames. ... Version 7 of the Java platform (current as of September 2012) refers to the latest APPNOTE.TXT for optional use of the ZIP64 extension to support large files and for indicating the use of UTF-8 (Appendix D). ... Version 1.0 of ODF (as published as ISO/IEC 26300:2006) referred to the APPNOTE.TXT version dated 1997-03-11 from Info-ZIP, because no appropriate version was made available publicly by PKWARE at the time because the version 6.2.0 referred to by the original ODF specification from OASIS had been superseded. ... In specific sections of version 6.3.3 of APPNOTE.TXT that relate to these two features, pointers are made to Section 10 of version 6.3.3 of APPNOTE.TXT, entitled \"Incorporating PKWARE Proprietary Technology into Your Product.\" ... Data integrity checks: A mandatory feature of the ZIP_PK format is the use of a 32-bit cyclic redundancy check (CRC) for each file using a specific CRC-32 algorithm.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIPの文字コードと文字化けの条件|ファイル名・パス制限の横断早見表 (https://www.conbu.jp/tool/filename-limits/zip.html)\nciteturn28search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 weeks ago; Crawled: last week; 汎用フラグ ビット11(Language encoding flag/EFS)を立てると、ファイル名とコメントはUTF-8でMUST(必須)エンコード ... 出典: PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT §4.4.4 general purpose bit flag ... 出典: PKWARE APPNOTE.TXT(規定)+ この環境での python 実機再現\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPKWARE Support (https://support.pkware.com/)\nciteturn28search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago;   * PKWARE Support ... High-performance encryption and compression software ...   * ### PK Transparent Server Agent - Public\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIP File Format (PKWARE) (https://ptacts.uspto.gov/ptacts/public-informations/petitions/1520098/download-documents?REDACTED)\nciteturn28search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.9 years ago; Crawled: 7.9 years ago; The Java platform does not support encryption. ... Details on the use of ZIP in OPC are in section 10 and Annex C of ISO/IEC 29500-2:2012. ... Version 1.0 of ODF (as published as ISO/IEC 26300:2006) referred to the APPNOTE.TXT version dated 1997-03-11 from Info-ZIP, because no appropriate version was made available publicly by PKWARE at the time because the version 6.2.0 referred to by the original ODF specification from OASIS had been superseded. ... Bearing in mind changes in technology since the original ZIP_PK, it appears to the compiler of this description that a common set of features for the most interoperable usage is emerging, including: the basic ZIP_PK structure with CRC-32 for checking file integrity, DEFLATE compression (or no compression), and support for long filenames, for filenames, etc., encoded in UTF-8, and for large files through ZIP64.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOffice Open (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=664fbfd9ec9de0ee00b3fda8d90d9f347dd675b3&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\nciteturn28search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; ZIP Appnote.txt ClarificationsBit ... section describing the Strong Encryption ... Table C–6, “Support for Extra field (variable size), PKWARE-reserved”, specifies the detailed production, ... 3Appnote.txt. ... Reserved for file stream and\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe .ZIP file format specification is formally named \"APPNOTE -.ZIP File Format Specification\" and it is published on the PKWARE.com website since the late 1990s.[11] Several versions of the specification were not published. Specifications of some features such as BZIP2 compression, strong encryption specification and others were published by PKWARE a few years after their creation. The URL of the online specification was changed several times on the PKWARE website. A summary of key advances in various versions of the PKWARE specification: (https://generationkpmg.pl/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Wonders_of_ZIP_file_format.pdf)\nciteturn28search15 [wordlim: 200] - 2.0: (1993)[11] File entries can be compressed with DEFLATE and use traditional PKWARE encryption (ZipCrypto). ... - 4.5: (2001)[12] Documented 64-bit zip format. ... - 5.2: (2003)[13][14] AES encryption support for SES (defined in APPNOTE 5.1 that was not published online) and AES from WinZip (\"AE-x\"); corrected version of RC2-64 supported for SES encryption. ... - 6.3.0: (2006)[17] Documented Unicode (UTF-8) filename storage.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nZIP (file format) (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZIP_%28file_format%29)\nciteturn28search16 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Specifications of some features such as BZIP2 compression, strong encryption specification and others were published by PKWARE a few years after their creation. ... * 6.3.0: (2006) Documented Unicode (UTF-8) filename storage. ... - File: APPNOTE.TXT - .ZIP File Format Specification Version: 4.0 Revised: 11/01/2000. ... ZIP File Format Specification Version: 6.3.10.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03184-60a2-7b03-bdab-fc6419c181fe","create_time":1787537208.210071}}}
