{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:09:53.192Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_03c0a296a55ba1de016a8ba7e1cb2087d28db69a85ed6b4add","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9F1iykAETXTdoy0Ih9t5dcnG","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\\n@@\\n - byte-preserving XML intake recognizes UTF-8, UTF-16, UTF-32, ISO-8859, Windows, CJK, and other legacy declarations across direct uploads, Data URLs, loose dependency assembly, and ZIP entries. XML-standard `ISO-10646-UCS-2` and `ISO-10646-UCS-4` aliases map onto the signature-aware UTF-16/32 decoders instead of being rejected as unknown; generic aliases accept either byte order only when the BOM or leading XML signature agrees. A production `iconv-lite` fallback extends Node's narrower WHATWG decoder set with allowlisted `ISO-8859-16`/Latin-10 and DOS `CP437`/`CP775`/`CP850`/`CP852`/`CP858` IANA aliases without admitting transport codecs such as base64, hex, or UTF-7 as XML encodings. Supported multibyte encodings are decoded strictly: incomplete UTF-8, UTF-16, UTF-32, Shift_JIS, and other WHATWG sequences fail with `source_document_xml_encoding_invalid_bytes` instead of entering normalization as replacement characters. Data-URL charset metadata remains authoritative when an XML declaration is absent. Original-corpus API gates preserve representative Romanian, German, Baltic, Czech, Cyrillic, Japanese, simplified/traditional Chinese, Korean, and Euro labels through the complete release projection across memory, file, and SQLite alongside a big-endian UCS-2 Booklet, a little-endian UCS-4 Booklet, a UCS-4 IMS manifest inside ZIP, and malformed multibyte rejection\\n+- ZIP entry names honor their declared encoding boundary: legacy names without the language-encoding flag continue through CP437 or a valid Info-ZIP Unicode Path field, while bit-11 names must be valid UTF-8. A malformed flagged name rejects the complete archive as `source_document_zip_invalid` instead of being normalized with replacement characters, matching the Original's libzip-backed archive-open boundary\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\n@@\\n Strict XML byte-sequence validation now rejects malformed UTF-8, UTF-16,\\n UTF-32, Shift_JIS, and other supported WHATWG multibyte input before replacement\\n characters can reach normalization. A mixed-ZIP gate proves that the damaged\\n Unit and its dependent Booklet/roster are quarantined while a complete sibling\\n graph still stages across memory, file, and SQLite. This narrows the existing\\n partial encoding/XML/package rows without changing the rounded estimate.\\n+\\n+The ZIP filename boundary now also follows the Original's libzip behavior.\\n+Entries with the language-encoding flag require fatal UTF-8 decoding; one\\n+malformed flagged name rejects the complete package as\\n+`source_document_zip_invalid` rather than silently introducing a replacement\\n+character. Legacy CP437 names and correctly bound Info-ZIP Unicode Path fields\\n+remain accepted. This closes the identified archive-open differential inside\\n+the existing partial package-intake row and does not change the rounded\\n+estimate.\\n@@\\n-ZIP entry-name decoding now follows the archive flag instead of assuming every\\n-package is UTF-8. Bit-11 names remain UTF-8; legacy entries without that flag\\n-use the required CP437 mapping. A production API gate encodes\\n+ZIP entry-name decoding now follows the archive flag instead of assuming every\\n+package is UTF-8. Bit-11 names are decoded as strict UTF-8; malformed byte\\n+sequences invalidate the complete archive with the stable\\n+`source_document_zip_invalid` diagnostic, matching the Original's libzip-backed\\n+archive-open boundary. Legacy entries without that flag use the required CP437\\n+mapping. Production API gates reject a malformed flagged filename and encode\\n `units/Größe.xml` as raw CP437, references the Unicode path from the manifest,\\n and requires the resolved Unit XML to reach the staged runtime snapshot. The\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03184-60a2-7b03-bdab-fc6419c181fe","create_time":1787537375.753109}}}
