{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:16:28.905Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_03c0a296a55ba1de016a8ba97a519487d2b93b6e41ad509a04","status":"completed","call_id":"call_vVUuTqsuck18BDvfpDRoLxzE","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"nl -ba docs/PARITY.md | sed -n '47,116p'\\nnl -ba docs/PARITY.md | sed -n '131,148p'\\nnl -ba docs/PARITY.md | sed -n '1210,1231p'\\nnl -ba packages/application/src/index.ts | sed -n '15240,15262p'\\nnl -ba scripts/smoke-local-demo.mjs | sed -n '344,380p'\\ngit rev-parse HEAD\\ngit rev-parse origin/testcenter-rewrite-parity\\ngit status --short\\nshasum -a 256 docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":14000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03184-60a2-7b03-bdab-fc6419c181fe","create_time":1787537780.1338}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T02:16:29.057Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0318e-1081-7e40-a711-b63a58586700","call_id":"call_vVUuTqsuck18BDvfpDRoLxzE","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n    47\t\n    48\tPriority:\n    49\t\n    50\t- `P0`: blocks credible test delivery or migration from the original\n    51\t- `P1`: required for operational parity in a first production rollout\n    52\t- `P2`: important follow-up after the first controlled rollout\n    53\t\n    54\t## Audited completion snapshot\n    55\t\n    56\tAgainst the release and master revisions above, the rounded engineering\n    57\testimate is **93% functional parity (uncertainty about +/- 3 percentage\n    58\tpoints)**. The estimate weights P0/P1/P2 capabilities 5/3/1, treats every\n    59\t`done` row as complete, and scores each `partial` row from its concrete\n    60\tremaining behavior rather than from source-line counts. It therefore includes\n    61\tthe newly recorded 18.2 security requirements, including the now-complete\n    62\tpassword-policy, proof-of-work, HSTS, and secret-file bootstrap boundaries, and\n    63\tdoes not treat test-only upstream churn as missing application behavior. This\n    64\tis a dated planning estimate, not evidence that every production package or\n    65\tdeployment has passed acceptance.\n    66\t\n    67\tA fresh upstream fetch on 2026-08-24 confirmed that the latest Original remains\n    68\t`origin/master` at `6455e265421777124f379090257365b70b21641f`, still 68 commits\n    69\tafter 18.2.0. No additional product delta therefore changes the weighted\n    70\testimate. The audit did, however, turn one previously broad \"rare file-graph\"\n    71\tgap into the explicit mixed-ZIP acceptance requirement below. That requirement\n    72\tis now closed. Its implementation raises the evidence within the already-\n    73\tpartial package-intake, XML-validation, and dependency-graph rows, but does not\n    74\tadd or complete a separately weighted capability and therefore does not change\n    75\tthe rounded 93% estimate. Operator-guided resolution of ambiguous loose\n    76\tworkspace dependencies is now closed as well: the import diagnostic exposes\n    77\tthe exact candidate source-package IDs, Angular requires an explicit choice,\n    78\tand the server validates that choice before continuing the remaining automatic\n    79\ttransitive closure. This likewise strengthens existing partial rows without\n    80\tchanging their weighted status or the rounded estimate. Selected deletion\n    81\tgraphs are now closed for the same bounded workspace-file workflow: the batch\n    82\tresolves roots before their selected dependencies regardless of request order,\n    83\tsupports multiple dependency levels, and retains a dependency when its selected\n    84\troot fails confirmation or another guard. This removes the known\n    85\tearlier-mutation deletion gap but leaves concurrent graph changes and broader\n    86\treplacement graphs in the partial capability, so the rounded estimate remains\n    87\t93%. The explicit non-WHATWG XML decoder allowlist now also covers ten\n    88\tadditional IANA-registered DOS/IBM families (`IBM775`, `IBM855`, `IBM857`,\n    89\t`IBM860`, `IBM861`, `IBM862`, `IBM863`, `IBM864`, `IBM865`, and `IBM869`) with their\n    90\tregistered XML-name-compatible aliases. This further narrows the rare-encoding\n    91\tpart of the existing partial package-intake row without admitting transport\n    92\tcodecs or changing the rounded estimate.\n    93\t\n    94\tStrict XML byte-sequence validation now rejects malformed UTF-8, UTF-16,\n    95\tUTF-32, Shift_JIS, and other supported WHATWG multibyte input before replacement\n    96\tcharacters can reach normalization. A mixed-ZIP gate proves that the damaged\n    97\tUnit and its dependent Booklet/roster are quarantined while a complete sibling\n    98\tgraph still stages across memory, file, and SQLite. This narrows the existing\n    99\tpartial encoding/XML/package rows without changing the rounded estimate.\n   100\t\n   101\tThe ZIP filename boundary now also follows the Original's libzip behavior.\n   102\tEntries with the language-encoding flag require fatal UTF-8 decoding; one\n   103\tmalformed flagged name rejects the complete package as\n   104\t`source_document_zip_invalid` rather than silently introducing a replacement\n   105\tcharacter. Legacy CP437 names and correctly bound Info-ZIP Unicode Path fields\n   106\tremain accepted. This closes the identified archive-open differential inside\n   107\tthe existing partial package-intake row and does not change the rounded\n   108\testimate.\n   109\t\n   110\tThe production STARS recovery gate now also closes the known browser-outbox\n   111\tcapacity-loss case: once all 200 validated slots are occupied, a 201st\n   112\tindependent Unit is rejected with visible failed-save and retry behavior rather\n   113\tthan evicting an older secured response. Abrupt process termination remains in\n   114\tthe already-partial recovery capability, so this additional evidence does not\n   115\tchange the rounded 93% estimate.\n   116\t\n   131\t## Current remaining-work queue\n   132\t\n   133\tThe capability matrix below is authoritative for completion status. This queue\n   134\tcontains only work that is still open after the 2026-08-24 upstream audit;\n   135\tparticipant execution modes, attachments/QR capture, and instance branding are\n   136\tno longer listed because their matrix rows are `done`.\n   137\t\n   138\t| Order | Priority | Remaining capability | Concrete acceptance gap |\n   139\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   140\t| 1 | P0 | Production package and dependency corpus | Add further real production packages and cover the remaining rare XML lexical facets, encodings, archive layouts, and ambiguous/cross-file dependency graphs without weakening quarantine or duplicate protection. The IANA-registered Baltic IBM775 family and strict malformed multibyte rejection are now covered through the durable-store matrix. |\n   141\t| 2 | P0 | Adaptive and runtime-policy corpus | Exercise broader production coding schemes and nested combinations of adaptive states, timers, completeness locks, code gates, and leave-once navigation across the durable-store and browser gates. |\n   142\t| 3 | P0 | Verona Player-family and API hardening | Add further production Player families and metadata/API edge cases; close interactive state parity for the currently feasibility-only IB runtime snapshot while retaining byte/range delivery, restoration, and visible failure behavior. |\n   143\t| 4 | P0 | Interruption and recovery at production scale | The complete current Original STARS path now proves 28-Unit foreground recovery, two simultaneously interrupted 28-Unit runs across an actual hard reload, run-isolated draining, a second hard reload after seven of 28 Units have already settled, page-close handoff, idempotent replay, queue cleanup, and lossless behavior at the 200-entry browser-storage boundary. Extend that production scale to abrupt browser/process termination that cannot be represented by an ordinary page reload or page-close event. |\n   144\t| 5 | P1 | Workspace batch edge cases | Add concurrent dependency-change and broader replacement graphs, including stale operator selections whose relationships change between readiness and mutation. Sequential upload mutation/collision behavior, the Original's single-file dependency deletion guard, and request-order-independent deletion of selected multi-level dependency graphs with failed-root retention are now closed. |\n   145\t| 6 | P1 | Additional system-check variants | Reconcile more original system-check definitions, report sets, and embedded Player families beyond the currently pinned 18.0 configurations. |\n   146\t| 7 | P2 | Remaining presentation combinations | Gate uncommon historical package-defined participant text and presentation combinations that are outside the complete current participant/monitor catalogs already implemented. |\n   147\t\n   148\t## Capability delivery evidence\n  1210\theaders, closing parser-differential ambiguity. Standard streaming ZIPs with\n  1211\tbit 3 set remain compatible: zero local placeholders plus a signed data\n  1212\tdescriptor are accepted while the payload is still bounded and verified using\n  1213\tthe authoritative central-directory values. Production API gates independently\n  1214\tcover corrupt payload metadata, all three local-header mismatches, and a\n  1215\tdeflated manifest/Booklet/Unit package whose entries use data descriptors;\n  1216\tinvalid XML entries fail staging with the stable\n  1217\t`source_document_zip_xml_unreadable` diagnostic instead of entering the\n  1218\tdependency graph as apparently valid content.\n  1219\t\n  1220\tZIP entry-name decoding now follows the archive flag instead of assuming every\n  1221\tpackage is UTF-8. Bit-11 names are decoded as strict UTF-8; malformed byte\n  1222\tsequences invalidate the complete archive with the stable\n  1223\t`source_document_zip_invalid` diagnostic, matching the Original's libzip-backed\n  1224\tarchive-open boundary. Legacy entries without that flag use the required CP437\n  1225\tmapping. Production API gates reject a malformed flagged filename and encode\n  1226\t`units/Größe.xml` as raw CP437, references the Unicode path from the manifest,\n  1227\tand requires the resolved Unit XML to reach the staged runtime snapshot. The\n  1228\tInfo-ZIP Unicode Path extra field (`0x7075`) is also honored when its version,\n  1229\tUTF-8 payload, and CRC-32 binding to the raw header name are valid; an invalid\n  1230\tbinding falls back to CP437 instead of redirecting dependency resolution. A\n  1231\tsecond gate resolves the non-CP437 path `units/測定.xml` through that field and\n 15240\t};\n 15241\t\n 15242\tconst decodeZipFileName = (\n 15243\t  fileNameBytes: Buffer,\n 15244\t  generalPurposeBitFlag: number,\n 15245\t  extraFields: Buffer = Buffer.alloc(0)\n 15246\t): string | null => {\n 15247\t  if ((generalPurposeBitFlag & 0x0800) !== 0) {\n 15248\t    try {\n 15249\t      return new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true }).decode(fileNameBytes);\n 15250\t    } catch {\n 15251\t      // PKWARE's language-encoding flag requires a valid UTF-8 filename. The\n 15252\t      // Original's libzip/ZipArchive boundary rejects the complete archive\n 15253\t      // instead of normalizing malformed bytes to replacement characters.\n 15254\t      return null;\n 15255\t    }\n 15256\t  }\n 15257\t\n 15258\t  const unicodePath = readZipUnicodePathExtraField(\n 15259\t    fileNameBytes,\n 15260\t    extraFields\n 15261\t  );\n 15262\t  if (unicodePath != null) {\n   344\t    undefined,\n   345\t    { timeout: 15_000 }\n   346\t  );\n   347\t\n   348\t  await page.goto(`${baseUrl}${demoParticipantPath}`, {\n   349\t    waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\"\n   350\t  });\n   351\t  await page.waitForFunction(\n   352\t    () => {\n   353\t      const status = document\n   354\t        .querySelector(\"#participantRouteStatus\")\n   355\t        ?.textContent?.trim();\n   356\t      const session =\n   357\t        document.querySelector(\"#participantRouteSessionId\")?.value ?? \"\";\n   358\t      return status === \"running\" && session.trim().length > 0;\n   359\t    },\n   360\t    undefined,\n   361\t    { timeout: 15_000 }\n   362\t  );\n   363\t  const firstParticipantSessionId = await page\n   364\t    .locator(\"#participantRouteSessionId\")\n   365\t    .inputValue();\n   366\t  for (const starterField of [\n   367\t    \"#participantWorkspaceKey\",\n   368\t    \"#participantLoginKey\",\n   369\t    \"#participantRouteGroupKey\",\n   370\t    \"#participantRouteBookletKey\"\n   371\t  ]) {\n   372\t    assert.equal(await page.locator(starterField).count(), 0);\n   373\t  }\n   374\t  await page.goto(`${baseUrl}${demoParticipantPath}`, {\n   375\t    waitUntil: \"domcontentloaded\"\n   376\t  });\n   377\t  await page.waitForFunction(\n   378\t    expectedSessionId => {\n   379\t      const status = document\n   380\t        .querySelector(\"#participantRouteStatus\")\n0069e4884b0c8a4bbdde0938d88b4dedc5d4a032\n0069e4884b0c8a4bbdde0938d88b4dedc5d4a032\n?? docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n7a2826bc8f1a9ffb92519a90f3784a6b1dbc27000892b21068a55a637a958a8a  docs/testcenter-thread-migration-process.pptx\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a03184-60a2-7b03-bdab-fc6419c181fe","create_time":1787537789.057928}}}
