{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T17:40:19.495Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08520c685d1a1132016a931980b6cc87d2b2f2551e84b5aafa","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6ATTi5aO7XFfecUhjmPoqvhl","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\"cmd\":\"node --check scripts/smoke-ui.mjs && git diff --check && git diff --stat && rg -n 'renderer crash|browser-process|complete browser-process|Interruption and recovery|persistent profile' docs/PARITY.md README.md scripts/smoke-ui.mjs | head -80\\nrg -n '^\\\\| [^|]+ \\\\| (done|partial|missing) \\\\|' docs/PARITY.md | rg -i 'recover|offline|verona|interrupt|browser'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":10000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788025213.325491}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T17:40:19.712Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04e9b-aa80-71d1-b90f-82a5ce4860cb","call_id":"call_6ATTi5aO7XFfecUhjmPoqvhl","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs | 306 ++++++++++++++++++++-------------------\n 1 file changed, 161 insertions(+), 145 deletions(-)\nscripts/smoke-ui.mjs:13348:  logStep(\"participant-original-stars-browser-process-crash-recovery\");\nscripts/smoke-ui.mjs:13457:            \"Timed out waiting for the Chromium browser-process crash signal.\"\nscripts/smoke-ui.mjs:13497:      \"The browser-process crash gate must not depend on a pagehide handoff.\"\nscripts/smoke-ui.mjs:13532:  stopAfter(\"participant-original-stars-browser-process-crash-recovery\");\nREADME.md:913:The STARS corpus retains the byte-exact metadata-2.0/API-6 Player from a fixed official Testbed commit and a radio-button definition from the matching 0.6.19 source tag as historical independent-family coverage. It also pins the current official 0.7.2 release and its byte-exact BUTTONS option-text definition from the same source tag; production SQLite/Chromium gates `stars-unit-definition@5.3`, persists its `iqb-standard@2.0` choice in JSON-string `responses`, and restores the selection after reload. Separately, the current Original Testcenter package pins the complete 0.6.40 Player/Unit/Voud/Vomd/28-alias Booklet/Testtakers graph. Its production SQLite/Chromium gate imports the unmodified assets, signs in through the original hot-return account, persists `iqb-standard@2.0` responses on aliases `1` and `2`, follows the Player's continue navigation, and restores the second selected option after reload. The dedicated `smoke:ui:stars-recovery` slice additionally proves that the bounded 200-entry browser outbox retains 56 alias-scoped responses from two valid participant runs across one actual hard reload with the active save route unavailable. It restores the visible response semantically after Player JSON reserialization, drains only that run with its visible Unit first, retains the other run exactly until its own session opens and drains visible-Unit-first, then mirrors a separate 28-Unit queue into IndexedDB on page close, replays it idempotently, and leaves both queues empty. A separate mid-drain reload settles seven of 28 responses, retains exactly the remaining 21 across the Player restart, tolerates the idempotent visible-Unit reserialization, and finishes with all server responses committed and the browser queue empty. A real Chromium renderer crash now proves that another complete 28-Unit queue remains in origin storage and drains after a fresh page in the same browser context without any `pagehide` handoff. At the storage boundary, a full 200-entry outbox rejects a 201st independent Unit instead of silently evicting an older response; the Participant sees the failed save, every secured entry remains byte-for-byte present, and an explicit retry persists the current answer after capacity is released.\ndocs/PARITY.md:124:than evicting an older secured response. A real Chromium renderer crash now\ndocs/PARITY.md:126:`pagehide` handoff. A complete browser-process kill plus persistent-profile\ndocs/PARITY.md:156:| 4 | P0 | Interruption and recovery at production scale | The complete current Original STARS path now proves 28-Unit foreground recovery, two simultaneously interrupted 28-Unit runs across an actual hard reload, run-isolated draining, a second hard reload after seven of 28 Units have already settled, page-close handoff, idempotent replay, queue cleanup, lossless behavior at the 200-entry browser-storage boundary, and a real renderer crash that fires no `pagehide`. Extend the same gate to complete browser-process termination plus relaunch with a persistent profile. |\ndocs/PARITY.md:906:without a `pagehide` handoff. Complete browser-process termination plus relaunch\ndocs/PARITY.md:907:with a persistent profile remains the production-scale gap.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788025219.712464}}}
