{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T17:48:14.606Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04ea2-e98e-7891-a284-024a9a7df236","call_id":"call_vFYwI26LuzHQ0gcKVl8o8rF4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\ndocs/PARITY.md:4:`284a4ffcd9452d56dddd51939707ac7f646c3da7` (2026-04-20) as its broad baseline\ndocs/PARITY.md:10:`90ec58845d84d899fb993553d03767c072fdd05c` (2026-08-18) plus the complete\ndocs/PARITY.md:21:`65d28718eb6474cf5158206494096d32cd3393f9` (2026-08-20). The complete\ndocs/PARITY.md:65:estimate is **93% functional parity (uncertainty about +/- 3 percentage\ndocs/PARITY.md:86:the rounded 93% estimate. Operator-guided resolution of ambiguous loose\ndocs/PARITY.md:98:93%. The explicit non-WHATWG XML decoder allowlist now also covers ten\ndocs/PARITY.md:128:evidence does not change the rounded 93% estimate.\ndocs/PARITY.md:189:follow-up audit at `65d28718eb6474cf5158206494096d32cd3393f9` refreshes the\nREADME.md:737:- a pinned original Testcenter 14.3/15.1/15.2/17.4/17.6/18.0 compatibility corpus now imports both historical and current production-shaped packages, including both historical and current three-Booklet root Sample packages with the current two-SysCheck/expanded-roster graph, the historical 17-case and current 27-case `CY_Bklt_TC-*` Test-Controller packages, the complete legacy/current BookletConfig matrix, and the current Session-Management and Group-Monitoring packages. The current two-Booklet Session-Management graph activates with all five Units, Verona 6.0.5, and its byte-exact 12-login roster; password-free/protected entry, ordered multi-Booklet assignment, second codes, access windows, and Hot-Return versus Hot-Restart re-entry with response restoration run across memory, file, and SQLite. The current Controller corpus at `65d28718eb6474cf5158206494096d32cd3393f9` likewise activates all 27 current 18.0 booklets, their five current Units, Verona 6.0.5 Player, and the byte-exact current 36-login `CY_Logins_TestController.xml` roster in one workspace, while retaining the independently pinned historical package; its nine refactored navigation cases use only `toolbar_show_unit_list`. Official Demo variants, Review variants, Hot-Return, and Hot-Restart accounts gate mode policy, code/time enforcement, durable response return versus clean restart, and monitor inclusion across memory, file, and SQLite. The current Group-Monitoring package independently gates its empty legacy monitor password as a passwordless migration candidate, explicit creation with a replacement operator password, exact profile retention, group isolation, and participant-visible pause/resume/go-to/lock/unlock transitions across memory, file, and SQLite. The importer accepts the original `id-6.0` Verona-player reference as a version-checked legacy alias while retaining identity and version mismatch failures. Its real `Booklet2.xml` + `Unit2.xml` + coding scheme + Verona 6 dependency set gates both prebuilt-ZIP and loose multi-upload intake, immutable dependency retention, and raw-response adaptive routing end-to-end. The byte-exact current `CY_Bklt_Adap-1.xml` package, Verona 6.0.5 Player, and two-account `CY_Logins_Adap.xml` roster additionally gate the five official default/value/coder/Review-preset/Review-override scenarios across memory, file, and SQLite. The current two-Booklet/four-Unit Aspect graph and changed 18.0 roster likewise gate the new Unit, full dependency retention, symbol-keypad settings, second-code enforcement, and the real multi-booklet `testuser1` flow across all three stores. The complete official `@iqb/responses` 3.6.0 `test/coding/derive` tree is additionally pinned through 11 scheme variants and all 23 byte-exact inputs/outcomes. A combined compatibility package gates `CONCAT_CODE`, `COPY_VALUE`, `MANUAL`, all four `SOLVER` variants, `SUM_CODE`, `SUM_SCORE`, and `UNIQUE_VALUES`, including aliases, same-ID/no-alias solvers, dependency failures, arrays, copied unset values, partial inputs, explicit zeroes, and every official status/value/code/score route through import, server coding, adaptive routing, and raw-response retention across memory, file, and SQLite. The historical DAN `G231mm.xml` + `G231mm.voud` + metadata-free `IQBVisualUnitPlayerV2.99.2.html` graph now has prebuilt and loose intake gates plus a production SQLite/Chromium execution gate for its API-2.1 handshake, JSON-string `all` response, and reload restoration; dotted version suffixes resolve only as a conservative metadata-free filename fallback, and competing versions remain an explicit ambiguity. Its complete original three-unit Aspect booklet, IQB Aspect 2.12.3 player, and all Unit/Voud pairs add a production-sized import and browser handshake/save/navigation/restore gate, including a 16.17 MB media definition; operational monitor/system-check logins are excluded from participant import\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788025694.606078}}}
