{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T17:49:57.338Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08520c685d1a1132016a931bc3825487d2936a23531b256ba5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_l0pm1x3t0QTUaQJ26aiNhOT1","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({\n  cmd: \"rg -n \\\"93%|rounded estimate remains|Complete browser-process|Resume after reload|renderer crash|browser-process|Current remaining-work queue|Interruption and recovery\\\" docs/PARITY.md README.md\",\n  workdir: \"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",\n  yield_time_ms: 10000,\n  max_output_tokens: 12000\n});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788025794.085413}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T17:49:57.447Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04ea4-7b46-7453-8281-9a07d3376cbe","call_id":"call_l0pm1x3t0QTUaQJ26aiNhOT1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\nREADME.md:913:The STARS corpus retains the byte-exact metadata-2.0/API-6 Player from a fixed official Testbed commit and a radio-button definition from the matching 0.6.19 source tag as historical independent-family coverage. It also pins the current official 0.7.2 release and its byte-exact BUTTONS option-text definition from the same source tag; production SQLite/Chromium gates `stars-unit-definition@5.3`, persists its `iqb-standard@2.0` choice in JSON-string `responses`, and restores the selection after reload. Separately, the current Original Testcenter package pins the complete 0.6.40 Player/Unit/Voud/Vomd/28-alias Booklet/Testtakers graph. Its production SQLite/Chromium gate imports the unmodified assets, signs in through the original hot-return account, persists `iqb-standard@2.0` responses on aliases `1` and `2`, follows the Player's continue navigation, and restores the second selected option after reload. The dedicated `smoke:ui:stars-recovery` slice additionally proves that the bounded 200-entry browser outbox retains 56 alias-scoped responses from two valid participant runs across one actual hard reload with the active save route unavailable. It restores the visible response semantically after Player JSON reserialization, drains only that run with its visible Unit first, retains the other run exactly until its own session opens and drains visible-Unit-first, then mirrors a separate 28-Unit queue into IndexedDB on page close, replays it idempotently, and leaves both queues empty. A separate mid-drain reload settles seven of 28 responses, retains exactly the remaining 21 across the Player restart, tolerates the idempotent visible-Unit reserialization, and finishes with all server responses committed and the browser queue empty. A real Chromium renderer crash now proves that another complete 28-Unit queue remains in origin storage and drains after a fresh page in the same browser context without any `pagehide` handoff. At the storage boundary, a full 200-entry outbox rejects a 201st independent Unit instead of silently evicting an older response; the Participant sees the failed save, every secured entry remains byte-for-byte present, and an explicit retry persists the current answer after capacity is released.\ndocs/PARITY.md:65:estimate is **93% functional parity (uncertainty about +/- 3 percentage\ndocs/PARITY.md:86:the rounded 93% estimate. Operator-guided resolution of ambiguous loose\ndocs/PARITY.md:97:replacement graphs in the partial capability, so the rounded estimate remains\ndocs/PARITY.md:98:93%. The explicit non-WHATWG XML decoder allowlist now also covers ten\ndocs/PARITY.md:124:than evicting an older secured response. A real Chromium renderer crash now\ndocs/PARITY.md:126:`pagehide` handoff. A complete browser-process kill plus persistent-profile\ndocs/PARITY.md:128:evidence does not change the rounded 93% estimate.\ndocs/PARITY.md:144:## Current remaining-work queue\ndocs/PARITY.md:156:| 4 | P0 | Interruption and recovery at production scale | The complete current Original STARS path now proves 28-Unit foreground recovery, two simultaneously interrupted 28-Unit runs across an actual hard reload, run-isolated draining, a second hard reload after seven of 28 Units have already settled, page-close handoff, idempotent replay, queue cleanup, lossless behavior at the 200-entry browser-storage boundary, and a real renderer crash that fires no `pagehide`. Extend the same gate to complete browser-process termination plus relaunch with a persistent profile. |\ndocs/PARITY.md:906:without a `pagehide` handoff. Complete browser-process termination plus relaunch\ndocs/PARITY.md:1062:| Resume after reload/interruption | hot-return E2E flows | partial | P0 | running and participant-paused sessions resume and restore unit, Verona unit state, player page state, and response; monitor-paused sessions remain paused across direct Resume, session re-entry, and durable-store restart until a monitor continues them. The official Session-Management SM-7 fixture proves that repeated hot-return sign-in reuses the same session and run with its saved response, while SM-9 proves hot-restart creates a clean session and run. The production Chromium/SQLite Controller gate additionally exercises real `Test_Ctrl-3` and `Test_Ctrl-7` Player answers: Hot Return reuses the session/run and restores the selected answer, whereas Hot Restart creates clean session/run IDs while retaining the prior answer in its original run and filtered response export. A versioned browser outbox preserves unsent responses independently per Unit across transient disconnects and hard reloads, overlays the visible Unit before the Player remounts, then prioritizes that Unit and drains every remaining Unit after online re-entry. Page closure mirrors every pending Unit for the run into the Service-Worker queue instead of only the foreground draft. A production SQLite/Chromium gate proves three-Unit foreground recovery order plus three-Unit IndexedDB handoff and delivery across the complete active path of the official adaptive sample. The full Original STARS gate additionally retains two valid 28-Unit runs and all 56 responses across one hard reload, drains only the opened run, then proves the untouched second run drains visible-Unit-first when its own session opens. It separately reloads while a 28-Unit drain is in progress and proves that seven confirmed responses stay removed while exactly the remaining 21 survive and finish. After one online visit, the installable, versioned Service Worker also serves the cached Participant App-Shell and lazy route across a browser-proven offline reload, with a truthful connectivity notice; API state and test content remain network-authoritative, and a never-visited device still requires an initial connection |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788025797.44695}}}
