latest OpenAI API models. ... Create a CLI Codex can use Give Codex a composable command","title":"Codex use cases","url":"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases?category=data&category=engineering&category=front-end&category=integrations&category=ios&category=macos&search=Automation&task_type=analysis&task_type=code&task_type=testing&team=engineering&team=operations&team=sales"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn33search9","snippet":"JsonValue; object_ \"project.model_permissions\"constant\"project.model_permissions\"constant ... import com.openai.models.admin.organization.projects.modelpermissions.ProjectModelPermissions;","title":"Retrieve project model permissions | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/model_permissions/methods/retrieve"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn33search10","snippet":"file_object = openai.files.create(file: Pathname(\"input.jsonl\"), purpose: \"fine-tune\") ... To opt in and activate mTLS for an organization or project, follow the OpenAI Mutual TLS Beta Program","title":"OpenAI Ruby API library | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/ruby"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developers.openai.com","ref_id":"turn33search11","snippet":"$ openai admin:organization:projects:groups:roles list ... \"name\": \"API Project Key Manager\",","title":"List project group role assignments | OpenAI API Reference","url":"https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/groups/subresources/roles/methods/list"}]}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:23:53.034Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04efa-794a-7d01-84a6-d2c279c2fa84","call_id":"call_owGnaI1Se2GWIY3dykQELVAr","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/)\nciteturn33search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: today; # OpenAI for developers ... Discover what builders are creating with Codex and the OpenAI API, and build your own version.\n\n# OpenAI for developers\n\nDocs and resources to help you build with, for, and on OpenAI.\n\n## GPT-5.6: Lower prices and faster speeds.\n\nSol is now over 20% cheaper, Luna is 80% cheaper, and Terra is 20% cheaper, while Fast mode makes Sol up to 2.5× faster.\n\nRead more here.\n\nAPI Platform Use our APIs and models to build your own AI experiences. Codex Build and ship faster with our coding agent — everywhere you work. Plugins Extend ChatGPT and Codex with skills, MCP servers, and optional UI.\n\n## Codex use cases\n\nLearn how teams are using Codex to automate tasks, build apps and ship with confidence.\n\nExplore use cases (opens in a new tab)\n\nImage: Illustration of Codex workflows and use cases\n\n## Showcase\n\nDiscover what builders are creating with Codex and the OpenAI API, and build your own version.\n\nExplore demos\n\nImage: Illustration of polished OpenAI demo showcases\n\n## Featured\n\nImage\n\n## GPT Image 2 for image generation and editing\n\nGenerate and edit images with stronger instruction following, flexible sizes, and high-fidelity image inputs.\n\nRead the GPT Image 2 prompting guide\n\nImage\n\n### Codex for (almost) everything\n\nApril 16, 2026\n\nRealtime and audio Codex changelog Community page\n\n## Blog posts\n\nView all\n\nAutomating repetitive work at OpenAI with Codex How Runme and WebMCP turn recurring engineering tasks into reviewable, reusable workflows. Aug 25, 2026 Codex Scaling cyber defenders with Daybreak Use ChatGPT, Codex Security, and open-source tools to investigate threats, validate vulnerabilities, and move from findings to reviewed, verified fixes. Aug 21, 2026 Codex Codex as a platform: build on the open agent harness Build Codex into the products and workflows your users already know. Aug 19, 2026 Codex\n\nAsk AI\n\n## Docs agent\n\nLoading docs agent...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex use cases (https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases?category=automation&category=integrations&category=ios&category=knowledge-work&category=quality&task_type=analysis&team=engineering&team=finance&team=quality-engineering&team=research&team=sales)\nciteturn33search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # Codex Use Cases\n\n# Codex Use Cases\n\n[Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input] [Input: Search Codex use cases]\n\nWorkflow Analysis Knowledge Work\n\n## Use cases\n\nSort:Sort use cases Recommended\n\nTurn feedback into actions Synthesize feedback from multiple sources into a reviewable artifact. Data Integrations\n\nClean and prepare messy data Process tabular data without affecting the original. Data Knowledge Work\n\nQuery tabular data Ask a question about a CSV, spreadsheet, export, or data folder. Data Knowledge Work\n\nLearn a new concept Turn dense source material into a clear, reviewable learning report. Knowledge Work Data\n\nRun a deep security scan Search an authorized repository deeply for plausible vulnerabilities. Engineering Quality\n\nScan code changes for security Review a pull request or local diff for security regressions. Engineering Quality\n\nAnnotate scRNA-seq data Review single-cell QC, annotations, and UMAPs in one thread. Sciences Data\n\nPrioritize drug targets Rank drug targets across multiple evidence lanes. Sciences Data\n\nValidate bulk RNA-seq inputs Validate bulk RNA-seq inputs before differential expression. Sciences Data\n\nForecast cash flow Find the liquidity low point in an editable forecast workbook. Data Knowledge Work\n\nModel a DCF valuation Turn financial inputs into an editable valuation workbook. Data Knowledge Work\n\nReview budget vs. actuals Turn plan, actuals, and close notes into a variance workbook. Data Knowledge Work\n\nTurn meetings into follow-ups Convert Zoom meeting insights into actions across your tools. Automation Integrations\n\nAudit dependency incidents Turn a public package advisory into a safe repo-audit plan. Engineering Quality\n\n## No use cases match these filters\n\nTry clearing a few filters or searching for a broader term.\n\nAsk AI\n\n## Docs agent\n\nLoading docs agent...--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWebhooks | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/webhooks)\nciteturn33search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; # Webhooks ... Sent when an incoming API SIP session is available for Live acceptance.\n\nFor the complete documentation index, see llms.txt. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending `.md` to the page URL.\n\n# Webhooks\n\n##### Models Expand Collapse\n\nclass BatchCancelledWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a batch API request has been cancelled.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass BatchCompletedWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a batch API request has been completed.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass BatchExpiredWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a batch API request has expired.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass BatchFailedWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a batch API request has failed.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass EvalRunCanceledWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when an eval run has been canceled.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass EvalRunFailedWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when an eval run has failed.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass EvalRunSucceededWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when an eval run has succeeded.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass FineTuningJobCancelledWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a fine-tuning job has been cancelled.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass FineTuningJobFailedWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a fine-tuning job has failed.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass FineTuningJobSucceededWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a fine-tuning job has succeeded.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass LiveCallIncomingWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when an incoming API SIP session is available for Live acceptance. The same pending session can also emit `realtime.call.incoming`; the first successful Realtime or Live accept endpoint selects the runtime surface.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass RealtimeCallIncomingWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when an incoming API SIP session is available for Realtime acceptance. The same pending session can also emit `live.call.incoming`; the first successful Realtime or Live accept endpoint selects the runtime surface.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass ResponseCancelledWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a background response has been cancelled.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass ResponseCompletedWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a background response has been completed.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass ResponseFailedWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a background response has failed.\n\nView schema details\n\nclass ResponseIncompleteWebhookEvent:\n\nSent when a background response has been interrupted.\n\nView schema details--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModify project | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/methods/update)\nciteturn33search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; client.admin.organization.projects.update(string projectID, ProjectUpdateParams { external_key_id, geography, name } body, RequestOptions options?): Project { id, created_at, object, 5 more } ...       adminAPIKey: process.env['OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY'], // This is the default and can be omitted\n\n# Modify project\n\nclient.admin.organization.projects.update(string projectID, ProjectUpdateParams { external_key_id, geography, name } body, RequestOptions options?): Project { id, created_at, object, 5 more }\n\nPOST/organization/projects/{project_id}\n\nModifies a project in the organization.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nprojectID: string\n\nbody: ProjectUpdateParams { external_key_id, geography, name }\n\nView schema details\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nProject { id, created_at, object, 5 more }\n\nRepresents an individual project.\n\nid: string\n\nThe identifier, which can be referenced in API endpoints\n\ncreated_at: number\n\nThe Unix timestamp (in seconds) of when the project was created.\n\nformat unixtime\n\nobject: \"organization.project\"\n\nThe object type, which is always `organization.project`\n\narchived_at?: number | null\n\nThe Unix timestamp (in seconds) of when the project was archived or `null`.\n\nformat unixtime\n\nexternal_key_id?: string | null\n\nThe external key associated with the project.\n\nname?: string | null\n\nThe name of the project. This appears in reporting.\n\nresidency?: ProjectResidency\n\nThe residency configuration for the project.\n\nView schema details\n\nstatus?: string | null\n\n`active` or `archived`\n\n### Modify project\n\nTypeScript\n    \n    `import OpenAI from 'openai';\n    \n    const client = new OpenAI({\n      adminAPIKey: process.env['OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY'], // This is the default and can be omitted\n    });\n    \n    const project = await client.admin.organization.projects.update('project_id');\n    \n    console.log(project.id);`\n\n[Button: 200 example]\n    \n    `{\n      \"id\": \"id\",\n      \"created_at\": 0,\n      \"object\": \"organization.project\",\n      \"archived_at\": 0,\n      \"external_key_id\": \"external_key_id\",\n      \"name\": \"name\",\n      \"residency\": \"GLOBAL\",\n      \"status\": \"status\"\n    }`\n\n##### Returns Examples\n\n[Button: 200 example]\n    \n    `{\n      \"id\": \"id\",\n      \"created_at\": 0,\n      \"object\": \"organization.project\",\n      \"archived_at\": 0,\n      \"external_key_id\": \"external_key_id\",\n      \"name\": \"name\",\n      \"residency\": \"GLOBAL\",\n      \"status\": \"status\"\n    }`--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRetrieve project model permissions | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/python/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/model_permissions/methods/retrieve)\nciteturn33search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; admin.organization.projects.model_permissions.retrieve(str project_id) -> ProjectModelPermissions ...         admin_api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY\"),  # This is the default and can be omitted\n\n# Retrieve project model permissions\n\nadmin.organization.projects.model_permissions.retrieve(str project_id) -> ProjectModelPermissions\n\nGET/organization/projects/{project_id}/model_permissions\n\nReturns model permissions for a project.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nproject_id: str\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nclass ProjectModelPermissions: …\n\nRepresents the model allowlist or denylist policy for a project.\n\nmode: Literal[\"allow_list\", \"deny_list\"]\n\nWhether the project uses an allowlist or a denylist.\n\nView schema details\n\nmodel_ids: List[str]\n\nThe model IDs included in the model permissions policy.\n\nobject: Literal[\"project.model_permissions\"]\n\nThe object type, which is always `project.model_permissions`.\n\n### Retrieve project model permissions\n\nPython\n    \n    `import os\n    from openai import OpenAI\n    \n    client = OpenAI(\n        admin_api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY\"),  # This is the default and can be omitted\n    )\n    project_model_permissions = client.admin.organization.projects.model_permissions.retrieve(\n        \"project_id\",\n    )\n    print(project_model_permissions.model_ids)`\n    \n    `{\n        \"object\": \"project.model_permissions\",\n        \"mode\": \"allow_list\",\n        \"model_ids\": [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"o3\"\n        ]\n    }\n    `\n\n##### Returns Examples\n    \n    `{\n        \"object\": \"project.model_permissions\",\n        \"mode\": \"allow_list\",\n        \"model_ids\": [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"o3\"\n        ]\n    }\n    `--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList project user role assignments | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/users/subresources/roles/methods/list)\nciteturn33search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; $ openai admin:organization:projects:users:roles list ...                 \"name\": \"API Project Key Manager\",\n\n# List project user role assignments\n\n$ openai admin:organization:projects:users:roles list\n\nGET/projects/{project_id}/users/{user_id}/roles\n\nLists the project roles assigned to a user within a project.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\n--project-id: string\n\nThe ID of the project to inspect.\n\n--user-id: string\n\nThe ID of the user to inspect.\n\n--after: optional string\n\nCursor for pagination. Provide the value from the previous response’s `next` field to continue listing project roles.\n\n--limit: optional number\n\nA limit on the number of project role assignments to return.\n\n--order: optional \"asc\" or \"desc\"\n\nSort order for the returned project roles.\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nRoleListResource: object { data, has_more, next, object }\n\nPaginated list of roles assigned to a principal.\n\ndata: array of object { id, assignment_sources, created_at, 9 more }\n\nRole assignments returned in the current page.\n\nView schema details\n\nhas_more: boolean\n\nWhether additional assignments are available when paginating.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRetrieve project | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/methods/retrieve)\nciteturn33search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; client.admin.organization.projects.retrieve(string projectID, RequestOptions options?): Project { id, created_at, object, 5 more } ...       adminAPIKey: process.env['OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY'], // This is the default and can be omitted\n\n# Retrieve project\n\nclient.admin.organization.projects.retrieve(string projectID, RequestOptions options?): Project { id, created_at, object, 5 more }\n\nGET/organization/projects/{project_id}\n\nRetrieves a project.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nprojectID: string\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nProject { id, created_at, object, 5 more }\n\nRepresents an individual project.\n\nid: string\n\nThe identifier, which can be referenced in API endpoints\n\ncreated_at: number\n\nThe Unix timestamp (in seconds) of when the project was created.\n\nformat unixtime\n\nobject: \"organization.project\"\n\nThe object type, which is always `organization.project`\n\narchived_at?: number | null\n\nThe Unix timestamp (in seconds) of when the project was archived or `null`.\n\nformat unixtime\n\nexternal_key_id?: string | null\n\nThe external key associated with the project.\n\nname?: string | null\n\nThe name of the project. This appears in reporting.\n\nresidency?: ProjectResidency\n\nThe residency configuration for the project.\n\nView schema details\n\nstatus?: string | null\n\n`active` or `archived`\n\n### Retrieve project\n\nTypeScript\n    \n    `import OpenAI from 'openai';\n    \n    const client = new OpenAI({\n      adminAPIKey: process.env['OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY'], // This is the default and can be omitted\n    });\n    \n    const project = await client.admin.organization.projects.retrieve('project_id');\n    \n    console.log(project.id);`\n    \n    `{\n        \"id\": \"proj_abc\",\n        \"object\": \"organization.project\",\n        \"name\": \"Project example\",\n        \"created_at\": 1711471533,\n        \"archived_at\": null,\n        \"status\": \"active\"\n    }\n    `\n\n##### Returns Examples\n    \n    `{\n        \"id\": \"proj_abc\",\n        \"object\": \"organization.project\",\n        \"name\": \"Project example\",\n        \"created_at\": 1711471533,\n        \"archived_at\": null,\n        \"status\": \"active\"\n    }\n    `--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModify project model permissions | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/python/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/model_permissions/methods/update)\nciteturn33search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; admin.organization.projects.model_permissions.update(str project_id, ModelPermissionUpdateParams**kwargs) -> ProjectModelPermissions ...         admin_api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY\"),  # This is the default and can be omitted\n\nCopy Markdown\n\n# Modify project model permissions\n\nadmin.organization.projects.model_permissions.update(str project_id, ModelPermissionUpdateParams**kwargs) -> ProjectModelPermissions\n\nPOST/organization/projects/{project_id}/model_permissions\n\nUpdates model permissions for a project.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nproject_id: str\n\nmode: Literal[\"allow_list\", \"deny_list\"]\n\nThe model permissions mode to apply.\n\nView schema details\n\nmodel_ids: Sequence[str]\n\nThe model IDs included in this permissions policy.\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nclass ProjectModelPermissions: …\n\nRepresents the model allowlist or denylist policy for a project.\n\nmode: Literal[\"allow_list\", \"deny_list\"]\n\nWhether the project uses an allowlist or a denylist.\n\nView schema details\n\nmodel_ids: List[str]\n\nThe model IDs included in the model permissions policy.\n\nobject: Literal[\"project.model_permissions\"]\n\nThe object type, which is always `project.model_permissions`.\n\n### Modify project model permissions\n\nPython\n    \n    `import os\n    from openai import OpenAI\n    \n    client = OpenAI(\n        admin_api_key=os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY\"),  # This is the default and can be omitted\n    )\n    project_model_permissions = client.admin.organization.projects.model_permissions.update(\n        project_id=\"project_id\",\n        mode=\"allow_list\",\n        model_ids=[\"string\"],\n    )\n    print(project_model_permissions.model_ids)`\n    \n    `{\n        \"object\": \"project.model_permissions\",\n        \"mode\": \"deny_list\",\n        \"model_ids\": [\n            \"o3\"\n        ]\n    }\n    `\n\n##### Returns Examples\n    \n    `{\n        \"object\": \"project.model_permissions\",\n        \"mode\": \"deny_list\",\n        \"model_ids\": [\n            \"o3\"\n        ]\n    }\n    `--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex use cases (https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases?category=data&category=engineering&category=front-end&category=integrations&category=ios&category=macos&search=Automation&task_type=analysis&task_type=code&task_type=testing&team=engineering&team=operations&team=sales)\nciteturn33search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Upgrade your API integration Upgrade your app to the latest OpenAI API models. ... Create a CLI Codex can use Give Codex a composable command for an API, log source, export, or team script.\n\n# Codex Use Cases\n\n[Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input][Input] [Input: Search Codex use cases]\n\nWorkflow Analysis Knowledge Work\n\n## Use cases\n\nSort:Sort use cases Recommended\n\nSet up a teammate Give Codex a durable view of your work so it can notice what changed. Automation Integrations\n\nTurn feedback into actions Synthesize feedback from multiple sources into a reviewable artifact. Data Integrations\n\nClean and prepare messy data Process tabular data without affecting the original. Data Knowledge Work\n\nQuery tabular data Ask a question about a CSV, spreadsheet, export, or data folder. Data Knowledge Work\n\nUnderstand large codebases Trace request flows, map unfamiliar modules, and find the right files fast. Engineering Analysis\n\nBuild a Mac app shell Use Codex to build a Mac-native SwiftUI app shell with a sidebar, detail pane, inspector... macOS Code\n\ncite9†Make granular UI changes Use Codex-Spark for fast, focused UI iteration in an existing app. \nRemediate a vulnerability backlog Turn reviewed findings into minimal fixes with regression evidence. Engineering Quality\n\nRun a deep security scan Search an authorized repository deeply for plausible vulnerabilities. Engineering Quality\n\nScan code changes for security Review a pull request or local diff for security regressions. Engineering Quality\n\nRun code migrations Migrate legacy stacks in controlled checkpoints. Engineering Code\n\nRefactor SwiftUI screens Use Codex to split an oversized SwiftUI screen into small subviews without changing behavior... iOS Code\n\nDraft PRDs from internal context Create product requirements documents from Linear, Slack, source documents, and meeting notes. Integrations Knowledge Work\n\nForecast cash flow Find the liquidity low point in an editable forecast workbook. Data Knowledge Work\n\nModel a DCF valuation Turn financial inputs into an editable valuation workbook. Data Knowledge Work\n\n【35†Review budget vs. actuals Turn plan, actuals, and close notes into a variance workbook. Data Knowledge Work Follow a goal Give Codex a durable objective for long-running work. Engineering Automation\n\nAdd evals to your AI application Use Codex to turn expected behavior into a Promptfoo eval suite. Evaluation Quality\n\nTurn user stories into UI mocks Convert product feedback, issue threads, and design context into mockups your team can react... Integrations Knowledge Work\n\nBring your app to ChatGPT Turn your use cases into focused apps for ChatGPT. Integrations Code\n\nBuild React Native apps with Expo Go from a mobile-app idea to a working Expo app with the dedicated plugin. Mobile Engineering\n\nCreate a CLI Codex can use Give Codex a composable command for an API, log source, export, or team script. Engineering Code\n\nPrioritize Slack action items Turn Slack threads and DMs into a ranked queue of next steps. Automation Integrations\n\nBuild and deploy internal apps Turn a team workflow into a hosted internal app with Sites. Front-end Integrations\n\nTurn meetings into follow-ups Convert Zoom meeting insights into actions across your tools. Automation Integrations\n\nAudit dependency incidents Turn a public package advisory into a safe repo-audit plan. Engineering Quality\n\nPrepare meeting briefs Turn calendar context into an agenda and notes plan. Integrations Knowledge Work\n\nRun event playbooks Create repeatable workflows for event program management. Integrations Knowledge Work\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRetrieve project model permissions | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/java/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/model_permissions/methods/retrieve)\nciteturn33search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; JsonValue; object_ \"project.model_permissions\"constant\"project.model_permissions\"constant ...     import com.openai.models.admin.organization.projects.modelpermissions.ProjectModelPermissions;\n\nCopy Markdown\n\n# Retrieve project model permissions\n\nProjectModelPermissions admin().organization().projects().modelPermissions().retrieve(ModelPermissionRetrieveParams params = ModelPermissionRetrieveParams.none(), RequestOptions requestOptions = RequestOptions.none())\n\nGET/organization/projects/{project_id}/model_permissions\n\nReturns model permissions for a project.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\nModelPermissionRetrieveParams params\n\nOptional<String> projectId\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nclass ProjectModelPermissions:\n\nRepresents the model allowlist or denylist policy for a project.\n\nMode mode\n\nWhether the project uses an allowlist or a denylist.\n\nView schema details\n\nList<String> modelIds\n\nThe model IDs included in the model permissions policy.\n\nJsonValue; object_ \"project.model_permissions\"constant\"project.model_permissions\"constant\n\nThe object type, which is always `project.model_permissions`.\n\n### Retrieve project model permissions\n\nJava\n    \n    `package com.openai.example;\n    \n    import com.openai.client.OpenAIClient;\n    import com.openai.client.okhttp.OpenAIOkHttpClient;\n    import com.openai.models.admin.organization.projects.modelpermissions.ModelPermissionRetrieveParams;\n    import com.openai.models.admin.organization.projects.modelpermissions.ProjectModelPermissions;\n    \n    public final class Main {\n        private Main() {}\n    \n        public static void main(String[] args) {\n            OpenAIClient client = OpenAIOkHttpClient.fromEnv();\n    \n            ProjectModelPermissions projectModelPermissions = client.admin().organization().projects().modelPermissions().retrieve(\"project_id\");\n        }\n    }`\n    \n    `{\n        \"object\": \"project.model_permissions\",\n        \"mode\": \"allow_list\",\n        \"model_ids\": [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"o3\"\n        ]\n    }\n    `\n\n##### Returns Examples\n    \n    `{\n        \"object\": \"project.model_permissions\",\n        \"mode\": \"allow_list\",\n        \"model_ids\": [\n            \"gpt-4.1\",\n            \"o3\"\n        ]\n    }--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOpenAI Ruby API library | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/ruby)\nciteturn33search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago;     file_object = openai.files.create(file: Pathname(\"input.jsonl\"), purpose: \"fine-tune\") ... To opt in and activate mTLS for an organization or project, follow the OpenAI Mutual TLS Beta Program guide. ...     approved_hosts = [\"mtls.auth.openai.com\", api_host].freeze\n## Webhook Verification\n\nVerifying webhook signatures is optional but encouraged.\n\nFor more information about webhooks, see the API docs.\n\n### Parsing webhook payloads\n\nFor most use cases, you will likely want to verify the webhook and parse the payload at the same time. To achieve this, we provide the method `client.webhooks.unwrap`, which parses a webhook request and verifies that it was sent by OpenAI. This method will raise an error if the signature is invalid.\n\nNote that the `body` parameter must be the raw JSON string sent from the server (do not parse it first). The `unwrap` method will parse this JSON for you into an event object after verifying the webhook was sent from OpenAI.\n    \n    `require 'sinatra'\n    require 'openai'\n    \n    # Set up the client with API credentials and the webhook secret\n    client = OpenAI::Client.new(\n      api_key: ENV.fetch('OPENAI_API_KEY'),\n      webhook_secret: ENV.fetch('OPENAI_WEBHOOK_SECRET')\n    )\n    \n    post '/webhook' do\n      request_body = request.body.read\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList project group role assignments | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/cli/resources/admin/subresources/organization/subresources/projects/subresources/groups/subresources/roles/methods/list)\nciteturn33search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; $ openai admin:organization:projects:groups:roles list ...                 \"name\": \"API Project Key Manager\",\n\nCopy Markdown\n\n# List project group role assignments\n\n$ openai admin:organization:projects:groups:roles list\n\nGET/projects/{project_id}/groups/{group_id}/roles\n\nLists the project roles assigned to a group within a project.\n\n##### Parameters Expand Collapse\n\n--project-id: string\n\nThe ID of the project to inspect.\n\n--group-id: string\n\nThe ID of the group to inspect.\n\n--after: optional string\n\nCursor for pagination. Provide the value from the previous response’s `next` field to continue listing project roles.\n\n--limit: optional number\n\nA limit on the number of project role assignments to return.\n\n--order: optional \"asc\" or \"desc\"\n\nSort order for the returned project roles.\n\n##### Returns Expand Collapse\n\nRoleListResource: object { data, has_more, next, object }\n\nPaginated list of roles assigned to a principal.\n\ndata: array of object { id, assignment_sources, created_at, 9 more }\n\nRole assignments returned in the current page.\n\nView schema details\n\nhas_more: boolean\n\nWhether additional assignments are available when paginating.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788031433.034649}}}
