{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:24:24.388Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04efa-f3c4-7682-b4c0-4d2e2bbfcd65","call_id":"call_W4pjTXnjdmouk9f6QIMV8gu8","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10654)\nTotal output lines: 221\n\n/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n12:- `approval_policy`, `sandbox_mode`, `permissions`, `permission profiles`, `network access`, `read-only`, `workspace-write`, `danger-full-access`, `security`, `cyber`: [Approvals, Sandboxing, and Security](#approvals-sandboxing-and-security)\n210:ChatGPT shows its progress and pauses when it needs information or approval.\n526:patch validation. **Daybreak Red** requires its own approval and provides\n599:Use `--approve-for-me` to enable [automatic approval\n683:and approval. Read the [July 29 sign-in\n905:per-chat or cross-chat MCP approval choices on iOS.\n925:explicit approval before it uses that access on a website.\n1054:#### Let Codex operate the browser and review approvals\n1058:reproduce issues and verify fixes. Eligible approval requests can also go\n1059:through [automatic approval review](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/sandboxing/auto-review),\n1602:          Cyber](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/cyber-safety#trusted-access-for-cyber) approval.\n1604:          separate approval and provisioning.\n1827:Configuration is one of the main ways to make Codex behave more consistently across sessions and surfaces. For example, you can set defaults for model choice, reasoning effort, sandbox mode, approval policy, profiles, and MCP setup.\n1837:Codex ships with operating level sandboxing and has two key knobs that you can control. Approval mode determines when Codex asks for your permission to run a command and sandbox mode determines if Codex can read or write in the directory and what files the agent can access.\n1839:If you're new to coding agents, start with the default permissions. Keep approval and sandboxing tight by default, then loosen permissions only for trusted repos or specific workflows once the need is clear.\n2181:#### Approvals and sandbox controls\n2186:local Codex sandbox or approval-mode control. Subagents use the tools available\n2193:In interactive CLI sessions, approval requests can surface from inactive agent\n2194:threads even while you are looking at the main thread. The approval overlay\n2198:In non-interactive flows, or whenever a run can't surface a fresh approval, an\n2199:action that needs new approval fails and Codex surfaces the error back to the\n2203:child. That includes sandbox and approval choices you set interactively during\n2711:- [Hooks](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks): Run custom commands when Codex emits lifecycle events.\n2834:review or approval.\n2955:[sandbox and approval policy](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/sandboxing) and pauses when it\n2956:needs a decision. With [automatic approval\n3222:- Ask for a plan when the approach matters. Require your approval before ChatGPT\n3288:Codex follows your approval policy before continuing.\n3645:## Approvals, Sandboxing, and Security\n3647:<a id=\"approvals-sandboxing-and-security\"></a>\n3649:Sandbox behavior, approvals, cyber-safety, and security-specific guidance.\n4036:local operating-system permissions and don't pause for approval. Scan\n4410:approval. Before you start, review [Local scan\n5468:uses the `codex_security_scan` filesystem profile and sets `approvalPolicy` to\n5471:request interactive approval.\n5474:`approval_policy`, `sandbox_mode`, and filesystem permissions, can't replace\n5760:- Keep non-interactive approval settings in nested deep scan workers.\n5947:- Return the selected findings to Codex for review and approval instead of\n6261:  JSON, CSV, SARIF, an approval-gated Linear, GitHub, or Jira issue, or a private\n6310:with your local operating-system permissions and never pauses for approval.\n6709:approval policy. See [Local scan\n6797:  duplicates and waits for your approval before writing.\n6911:and approval of the complete content. Treat a draft advisory description as\n6913:exploit details before approval.\n6915:Review and approve external actions in the Codex conversation. Approval\n7320:required approvals.\n8104:the runner's local permissions and don't pause for approval. Scan processes\n9101:  before approving them and keep [Codex approval and security\n9102:  policies](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security) in place.\n9266:### Agent approvals & security\n9268:Source: [Agent approvals & security](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security.md)\n9272:This page covers how to operate Codex safely, including sandboxing, approvals,\n9276:By default, the agent runs with network access turned off. Locally, Codex uses an OS-enforced sandbox that limits what it can touch (typically to the current workspace), plus an approval policy that controls when it must stop and ask you before acting.\n9282:#### Sandbox and approvals\n9287:- **Approval policy**: When Codex must ask you before it executes an action (for example, leaving the sandbox, using the network, or running commands outside a trusted set).\n9292:- **Codex CLI / IDE extension**: OS-level mechanisms enforce sandbox policies. Defaults include no network access and write permissions limited to the active workspace. You can configure the sandbox, approval policy, and network settings based on your risk tolerance.\n9294:In the `Auto` preset (for example, `--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request`), Codex can read files, make edits, and run commands in the working directory automatically.\n9296:Codex asks for approval to edit files outside the workspace or to run commands that require network access. If you want to chat or plan without making changes, switch to `read-only` mode with the `/permissions` command.\n9298:Codex can also elicit approval for app (connector) tool calls that advertise side effects, even when the action isn't a shell command or file change. Destructive app/MCP tool calls always require approval when the tool advertises a destructive annotation (unless the tool advertises a read annotation, which takes priority).\n9455:You can also control the [web search tool](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/tools-web-search) without granting full network access to spawned commands. Codex defaults to using a web search cache to access results. The cache is an OpenAI-maintained index of web results, so cached mode returns pre-indexed results instead of fetching live pages. This reduces exposure to prompt injection from arbitrary live content, but you should still treat web results as untrusted. If you are using `--yolo` or another [full access sandbox setting](#common-sandbox-and-approval-combinations), web search defaults to live results. Use `--search` or set `web_search = \"live\"` to allow live browsing, or set it to `\"disabled\"` to turn the tool off:\n9470:  - Version-controlled folders: `Auto` (workspace write + on-request approvals)\n9476:  - `codex --sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request`\n9477:  - `codex --sandbox read-only --ask-for-approval on-request`\n9489:#### Run without approval prompts\n9491:You can disable approval prompts with `--ask-for-approval never` or `-a never` (shorthand).\n9495:If you need Codex to read files, make edits, and run commands with network access without approval prompts, use `--sandbox danger-full-access` (or the `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` flag). Use caution before doing so.\n9497:For a middle ground, `approval_policy = { granular = { ... } }` lets you keep specific approval prompt categories interactive while automatically rejecting others. The granular policy covers sandbox approvals, execpolicy-rule prompts, MCP prompts, `request_permissions` prompts, and skill-script approvals.\n9499:#### Automatic approval reviews\n9501:By default, approval requests route to you:\n9504:approvals_reviewer = \"user\"\n9507:Automatic approval reviews apply when approvals are interactive, such as\n9508:`approval_policy = \"on-request\"` or a granular approval policy. Set\n9509:`approvals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"` to route eligible approval requests\n9513:approval_policy = \"on-request\"\n9514:approvals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\n9521:The reviewer evaluates only actions that already need approval, such as sandbox\n9546:can constrain it with `allowed_approvals_reviewers`.\n9548:#### Common sandbox and approval combinations\n9552:| Auto (preset)                                                     | _no flags needed_ or `--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request`                                                      | Codex can read files, make edits, and run commands in the workspace. Codex requires approval to edit outside the workspace or to access network. |\n9553:| Safe read-only browsing                                           | `--sandbox read-only --ask-for-approval on-request`                                                                                 | Codex can read files and answer questions. Codex requires approval to make edits, run commands, or access network.                               |\n9554:| Read-only non-interactive (CI)                                    | `--sandbox read-only --ask-for-approval never`                                                                                      | Codex can only read files; never asks for approval.                                                                                              |\n9555:| Automatically edit but ask for approval to run untrusted commands | `--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval untrusted`                                                                            | Codex can read and edit files but asks for approval before running untrusted commands.                                                           |\n9556:| Auto-review mode                                                  | `--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request -c approvals_reviewer=auto_review` or `approvals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"` | Same sandbox boundary as standard on-request mode, but eligible approval requests are reviewed by Auto-review instead of surfacing to the user.  |\n9557:| Dangerous full access                                             | `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` (alias: `--yolo`)                                                                      | No sandbox; no approvals _(not recommended)_                                                                                                     |\n9561:With `--ask-for-approval untrusted`, Codex runs only known-safe read operations automatically. Commands that can mutate state or trigger external execution paths (for example, destructive Git operations or Git output/config-override flags) require approval.\n9565:For the broader configuration workflow, see [Config basics](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-basic), [Advanced Config](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced#approval-policies-and-sandbox-modes), and the [Configuration Reference](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference).\n9568:# Always ask for approval mode\n9569:approval_policy = \"untrusted\"\n9577:# Optional: granular approval policy\n9578:# approval_policy = { granular = {\n9579:#   sandbox_approval = true,\n9583:#   skill_approval = false\n9591:approval_policy = \"on-request\"\n9597:approval_policy = \"never\"\n9632:This ensures the IDE extension inherits Linux sandbox semantics for commands, approvals, and filesystem access even when the host OS is Windows. Learn more in the [WSL guide](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/windows/wsl).\n9646:In that case, configure your Docker container to provide the isolation you need, then run `codex` with `--sandbox danger-full-access` (or the `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` flag) inside the container.\n9656:`--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` inside the container, a malicious\n9710:- When enabled, Codex emits structured log events covering chats, API requests, SSE/WebSocket stream activity, user prompts (redacted by default), tool approval decisions, and tool results.\n9750:- `codex.conversation_starts` (model, reasoning settings, sandbox/approval policy)\n9769:- Review events periodically for approval/sandbox changes and unexpected tool executions.\n9771:OTel is optional and designed to complement, not replace, the sandbox and approval protections described above.\n9781:Auto-review replaces manual approval at the sandbox boundary with a separate\n9783:the same approval policy and the same network and filesystem limits. The\n9786:Auto-review only applies when approvals are interactive. In practice, that\n9787:means `approval_policy = \"on-request\"` or a granular approval policy that\n9788:still surfaces the relevant prompt category. With `approval_policy = \"never\"`,\n9809:2. When it needs to cross the sandbox boundary, it requests approval.\n9810:3. If `approvals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"`, Codex routes that approval request\n9819:changes how Codex handles actions that already need approval.\n9823:Auto-review evaluates approval requests that would otherwise pause for a human.\n9829:- MCP or app tool calls that require approval based on their tool annotations\n9830:  or configured approval mode.\n9837:Computer Use is a separate case. App approvals for Computer Use still surface\n9854:per user with local [`[auto_review].policy`](/codex/config-file/config-advanced#approval-policies-and-sandbox-modes).\n9861:The reviewer sees a compact transcript plus the exact approval request. That\n9863:calls and tool outputs, and the action now being proposed for approval. It can\n9894:recent denials per task. That approval is narrow: it applies to the exact\n9897:Codex injects a developer-scoped approval marker for that exact action. The\n9912:[`[auto_review].policy`](/codex/config-file/config-advanced#approval-policies-and-sandbox-modes)\n9945:approval_policy = \"on-request\"\n9946:approvals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\n9975:allowed_approval_policies = [\"on-request\"]\n9976:allowed_approvals_reviewers = [\"auto_review\"]\n10005:`[auto_review].policy`. Keep `approval_policy = \"on-request\"` or another\n10006:eligible interactive approval policy and keep an enforceable sandbox boundary.\n10007:With `approval_policy = \"never\"`, `:danger-full-access`, or `--yolo`, an action\n10008:can avoid creating the boundary-crossing approval request that review requires.\n10012:`decision = \"prompt\"`, or configure sensitive MCP tools to require approval,\n10019:Agents SDK harnesses, use [Guardrails and human review](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/guardrails-approvals#review-cybersecurity-actions-before-execution).\n10030:  [`writable_roots`](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced#approval-policies-and-sandbox-modes)\n10083:Request **Daybreak access** through [Trusted Access for Cyber](https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001258-trusted-access-for-cyber). Access depends on approval and provisioning for your specific identity or service, ChatGPT workspace or API organization and project, authorized offering and model, and allowed product surface.\n10088:Submitting an application or completing identity verification doesn't guarantee approval.\n10090:Applying, verifying your identity, or receiving approval for Daybreak Blue\n10092:offering requires separate approval and provisioning.\n10121:For most work, start with **Ask for approval**. It lets ChatGPT work within the\n10130:**Ask for approval** is always available. To add **Approve for me** (called\n10144:- **Approvals** determine when ChatGPT pauses before an action or sends the\n10148:**Approve for me** keeps the same workspace boundary as **Ask for approval**;\n10605:execution. Use them together with approval policies and the separate controls\n10642:  use their own feature and approval controls.\n10672:you grant writes or outbound network access. Keep approval policy, secret\n10799:- Vulnerability disclosure, patch approval, and maintainer coordination.\n10800:- Stop conditions and actions that require explicit human approval.\n10807:approval_policy = \"on-request\"\n10808:approvals_reviewer = \"auto_review\"\n10852:Avoid `:danger-full-access` and `--yolo` for cybersecurity workflows. Fu…2654 tokens truncated…                                                     |         | Who reviews eligible approval prompts under `on-request` or granular approval policies. Defaults to `user`; `auto_review` uses the reviewer subagent. This setting doesn't change sandboxing or review actions already allowed inside the sandbox.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n11404:| `apps._default.approvals_reviewer`                            | `user \\| auto_review`                                                                                                                                                      |         | Default reviewer for app tool approval prompts unless overridden per app. When omitted, apps inherit the top-level `approvals_reviewer` value.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n11405:| `apps._default.default_tools_approval_mode`                   | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Default approval behavior for app tools without per-app or per-tool overrides.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n11409:| `apps..approvals_reviewer`                                    | `user \\| auto_review`                                                                                                                                                      |         | Reviewer for this app's tool approval prompts. Overrides `apps._default.approvals_reviewer`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n11410:| `apps..default_tools_approval_mode`                           | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Default approval behavior for tools in this app unless a per-tool override exists.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n11415:| `apps..tools..approval_mode`                                  | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Per-tool approval behavior override for a single app tool.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n11423:| `computer_use.windows.always_allowed_app_ids`                 | `array`                                                                                                                                                                    |         | Windows app identifiers that Computer Use can open without prompting. Apps not in the list require approval; remove saved entries from the ChatGPT desktop app's Computer Use settings.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n11443:| `features.hooks`                                              | `boolean`                                                                                                                                                                  |         | Enable lifecycle hooks loaded from `hooks.json` or inline `[hooks]` config. `features.codex_hooks` is a deprecated alias.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n11480:| `hooks`                                                       | `table`                                                                                                                                                                    |         | Lifecycle hooks configured inline in `config.toml`. Uses the same event schema as `hooks.json`; see the Hooks guide for examples and supported events.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n11483:| `hooks.[].hooks[].additionalContextLimit`                     | `integer`                                                                                                                                                                  |         | Approximate per-handler token threshold for saving oversized `additionalContext` to disk and showing the model a shorter preview. Defaults to `2500`; `0` passes the full context directly to the model. See [Large hook output](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks#large-hook-output).                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n11484:| `hooks.[].hooks[].async`                                      | `boolean`                                                                                                                                                                  |         | Run a command hook in the background without delaying the triggering operation. Defaults to `false`; `SessionEnd` always runs synchronously. See [Run hooks in the background](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks#run-hooks-in-the-background).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n11496:| `mcp_servers..default_tools_approval_mode`                    | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Default approval behavior for MCP tools on this server unless a per-tool override exists.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n11514:| `mcp_servers..tools..approval_mode`                           | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Per-tool approval behavior override for one MCP tool on this server.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n11612:| `plugins..mcp_servers..default_tools_approval_mode`           | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Default approval behavior for tools on a plugin-provided MCP server.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n11616:| `plugins..mcp_servers..tools..approval_mode`                  | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve`                                                                                                                                      |         | Per-tool approval behavior override for a plugin-provided MCP tool.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n11620:| `projects..trust_level`                                       | `string`                                                                                                                                                                   |         | Mark a project or worktree as trusted or untrusted (`\"trusted\"` \\| `\"untrusted\"`). Untrusted projects skip project-scoped `.codex/` layers, including project-local config, hooks, and rules.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n11649:| `tui.keymap..`                                                | `string \\| array`                                                                                                                                                          |         | Keyboard shortcut binding for a TUI action. Supported contexts include `global`, `chat`, `composer`, `editor`, `vim_normal`, `vim_operator`, `vim_text_object`, `pager`, `list`, and `approval`. Selected composer actions fall back to matching `tui.keymap.global` bindings; context-specific bindings take precedence when supported.                                                                                                                                                    |\n11712:| `allowed_approval_policies`                                 | `array`                               |         | Allowed values for `approval_policy` (for example `untrusted`, `on-request`, `never`, and `granular`).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n11713:| `allowed_approvals_reviewers`                               | `array`                               |         | Allowed values for `approvals_reviewer`, such as `user` and `auto_review`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n11718:| `apps`                                                      | `table`                               |         | Managed app requirements keyed by app identifier. Requirements can disable an app or constrain approval behavior for individual tools.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n11720:| `apps..tools..approval_mode`                                | `auto \\| prompt \\| writes \\| approve` |         | Set the managed approval mode for one app tool.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n11747:| `features.guardian_approval`                                | `boolean`                             |         | Pin Guardian approval availability on or off for managed users.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n11762:| `hooks.[].hooks[].additionalContextLimit`                   | `integer`                             |         | Approximate per-handler token threshold for saving oversized `additionalContext` to disk and showing the model a shorter preview. Defaults to `2500`; `0` passes the full context directly to the model. See [Large hook output](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks#large-hook-output).                                                                                                                                            |\n11763:| `hooks.[].hooks[].async`                                    | `boolean`                             |         | Run a command hook in the background without delaying the triggering operation. Defaults to `false`; `SessionEnd` always runs synchronously. See [Run hooks in the background](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks#run-hooks-in-the-background).                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788031464.388527}}}
