{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:26:30.745Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Die drei Setup-Dateien sind als `20e2d62` gepusht; lokaler und GitHub-Branch zeigen exakt denselben SHA. Aktuell steht die Checkpoint-Zahl erwartungsgemäß noch bei 0, weil diese Desktop-Sitzung vor der Hook-Aktivierung begonnen hat. Ich mache deshalb zusätzlich einen kleinen, schreibfreien Codex-Probelauf und verknüpfe ihn mit dem Setup-Commit, damit nicht nur die Konfiguration, sondern die vollständige Capture→Checkpoint→GitHub-Synchronisation belegt ist.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:26:30.745Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_08520c685d1a1132016a933264130c87d2b19460e848e69903","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Die drei Setup-Dateien sind als `20e2d62` gepusht; lokaler und GitHub-Branch zeigen exakt denselben SHA. Aktuell steht die Checkpoint-Zahl erwartungsgemäß noch bei 0, weil diese Desktop-Sitzung vor der Hook-Aktivierung begonnen hat. Ich mache deshalb zusätzlich einen kleinen, schreibfreien Codex-Probelauf und verknüpfe ihn mit dem Setup-Commit, damit nicht nur die Konfiguration, sondern die vollständige Capture→Checkpoint→GitHub-Synchronisation belegt ist."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788031576.663048,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:26:31.275Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08520c685d1a1132016a933266cfa887d28c439e9973fffa4f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_mZv5tWhwfrq9Pjx0fbWcLG0a","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"entire session attach --help\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:6000});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788031576.663048}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-29T19:26:31.388Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04efc-e3dc-7010-8e5a-3c838b964271","call_id":"call_mZv5tWhwfrq9Pjx0fbWcLG0a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\nAttach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in settings. Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a04e66-c772-7170-b7f2-4f6daa7e2bfb","create_time":1788031591.388938}}}
